{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And he said, My father, etc.</b> Now Isaac had not yet said anything to him; rather, he called out 'My father' and fell silent — for Isaac sensed that his father's desire was to offer him up as a burnt offering, and he thought, 'If so, he does not have mercy upon me as a father has mercy upon his children, and he has become to me like a cruel man' — for he did not yet know that this was the will of his Creator. Therefore he called him 'My father' to test him, to see whether he would answer him — for it was still fixed in his heart that he is his father — or whether he had already put it out of his mind as though he were not his son; for by this he wished to know who would be the one slaughtered. And when he answered him, 'Here I am, my son,' and showed him that all his yearning was still upon him, he said to him, 'If so, where is the lamb for the burnt offering?' And he said to him, 'Elohim will provide for Himself the lamb for the burnt offering, my son' — it was not I who chose you, but Elohim, and both you and I are obligated to His honor. Then 'the two of them walked on together' (Genesis 22:8) with one intention — to exclude [the possibility that] until now they had been divided in their minds."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:29:06.671178659Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}